  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Quinquagesima Sunday” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Jesus took aside the Twelve and said to them: Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem, and all that has been written by the prophets concerning the Son of Man will be accomplished. For He will be delivered to the Gentiles, mocked, scourged and spat upon; and after they have scourged Him, they will kill Him, and on the third day He will rise again. And they understood none of these things; this saying was hidden from them, and they did not understand what was being said. And it happened, as He drew near to Jericho, that a certain blind man was sitting by the wayside, begging. Hearing the crowd pass by, he asked what this meant. And they told him that Jesus of Nazareth was passing by. And he cried out, saying: Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me. And those who went ahead rebuked him so that he would be silent. But he cried out much more: Son of David, have mercy on me. And Jesus stood still and commanded that he be brought to Him. And when he had come near, He asked him, saying: What do you want Me to do for you? But he said: Lord, let me receive my sight. And Jesus said to him: Receive your sight; your faith has made you well. And immediately he saw and followed Him, glorifying God. And all the people, when they saw it, gave praise to God.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w004", "w005"], "anchor": "w004", "gloss": "Jesus took aside" }, { "words": ["w014", "w015"], "anchor": "w014", "gloss": "all things will be fulfilled" }, { "words": ["w016", "w017", "w018"], "anchor": "w016", "gloss": "that have been written" }, { "words": ["w024", "w025"], "anchor": "w024", "gloss": "For He will be delivered" }, { "words": ["w039", "w040"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "on the third day" }, { "words": ["w043", "w044", "w045", "w046"], "anchor": "w043", "gloss": "they understood none of these things" }, { "words": ["w048", "w049", "w050", "w051"], "anchor": "w051", "gloss": "this word was hidden" }, { "words": ["w055", "w056"], "anchor": "w056", "gloss": "they did not understand" }, { "words": ["w059", "w060", "w061"], "anchor": "w059", "gloss": "And it happened" }, { "words": ["w065", "w066"], "anchor": "w065", "gloss": "that a certain blind man" }, { "words": ["w080", "w081", "w082"], "anchor": "w080", "gloss": "And they told him" }, { "words": ["w102", "w103"], "anchor": "w102", "gloss": "But he" }, { "words": ["w104", "w105", "w106"], "anchor": "w104", "gloss": "cried out much more" }, { "words": ["w111", "w112", "w113", "w114"], "anchor": "w111", "gloss": "And Jesus stood still and commanded" }, { "words": ["w126", "w127", "w128"], "anchor": "w126", "gloss": "do you want Me to do for you" }, { "words": ["w133", "w134"], "anchor": "w133", "gloss": "let me receive my sight" }, { "words": ["w140", "w141"], "anchor": "w140", "gloss": "your faith" }, { "words": ["w142", "w143", "w144"], "anchor": "w142", "gloss": "has made you well" }] }
